# Line endings are normalized to LF in the repository and on checkout everywhere.
#
# Not a style preference. `dynquant/_legacy/` is a verbatim copy of the paper's
# code, kept as a reference oracle, and `tests/test_legacy_provenance.py` pins it
# by hash. Without this file a Windows checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` would
# rewrite those files on disk and the hash check would fail for a reason having
# nothing to do with the code. (The test also normalizes before hashing, so it is
# correct either way -- but a repository that disagrees with itself about line
# endings produces diffs where nothing changed, which is its own tax.)
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only entry points, which cmd.exe and older PowerShell hosts want CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary: never touched, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.safetensors binary
*.gguf binary
*.pt binary
*.bin binary
*.so binary
*.pyd binary
*.dylib binary
*.cubin binary
*.fatbin binary

# GitHub language statistics. The vendored research code is not this project's
# code and should not be counted as such; CUDA is, and GitHub does not detect it
# from `.cu` reliably in a mostly-Python repository.
packages/dynquant-core/src/dynquant/_legacy/** linguist-vendored
*.cu linguist-language=Cuda
*.cuh linguist-language=Cuda
